    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 30th with a clear focus on exploiting high-ceiling matchups against questionable starting pitching. **Trea Turner** (76.35) and **Kyle Schwarber** (75.20) represent our premier starts today, both benefiting significantly from an elite +19% SP skill advantage against Sasaki, whose 5.11 xERA suggests a volatile outing. **Yordan Alvarez** (73.62) remains a cornerstone play, boasting an elite 0.424 xwOBA that necessitates a start regardless of typical platoon considerations, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (71.82) is our primary catalyst for stolen base production; his matchup against Leahy in an aggressive, speed-oriented lineup spot makes him a high-efficiency asset today.\n\nBeyond the headliners, **Kazuma Okamoto** (69.87) receives a massive 16% park adjustment boost, fueling his status as a top-tier play against Young. Conversely, **Junior Caminero** (45.87) sits on the razor's edge of our utility spot; his score was suppressed by a daunting -19% SP skill penalty against the southpaw Detmers, yet he remains in the lineup due to a lack of more favorable alternatives. The most difficult bench decision involved **Caleb Durbin**, who finished at 39.98. While his contact profile is valuable, the combination of a sub-40 score and a bottom-tier batting order spot (9th) against Messick ultimately forced the optimizer to keep him on the pine to preserve our limited game caps for more high-leverage opportunities. We are proceeding with full confidence in this configuration, though we will continue to monitor lineups for **Carson Benge** and the rest of the crew to ensure no late-scratch weather or injury risks disrupt our expected output.",
